## First-time setup

```sh
./tools/bootstrap.sh
```

Clones the pinned third-party submodules these boards need. (Plain
`git submodule update --init` won't work here — a generated project has
`.gitmodules` but no git history, so there are no gitlinks for git to act on.)

## Build (target)

```sh
make
```
{% if boards | length > 1 %}
That builds `{{ boards[0] }}` until you select another board from the table above:

```sh
make configure BOARD=<preset>   # select it; plain make / make flash now use it
make BOARD=<preset>             # or build it once without changing the selection
make all-boards                 # or build every board
```

The selection is saved in `build/.board`; `make help` shows the current one and
`make distclean` resets it. Each board builds into its own `build/<preset>/`
directory, so they don't clobber each other.
{% endif %}
Output lands in `build/<preset>/{{ project_slug }}.elf` (plus `.bin`, `.hex`, `.map`).
`make help` lists every target.

The Makefile is a thin wrapper around the CMake presets. The equivalent by hand:

```sh
cmake --preset {{ boards[0] }}
cmake --build --preset {{ boards[0] }}
```

## Build & run tests (host)

Requires `ruby` on PATH (CMock uses it to generate mocks). Host tests are
board-independent — they exercise `src/app/` against mocked drivers.

```sh
make test
```

By hand:

```sh
cmake -S test -B build/host-test
cmake --build build/host-test
ctest --test-dir build/host-test
```

## Flash

Needs an ST-Link probe and one of the flash tools below on PATH (OpenOCD by default).

```sh
make flash{% if boards | length > 1 %}                      # or: make flash BOARD=<preset>{% endif %}
```

This rebuilds if needed, then programs, verifies and resets the board. Under
the hood it is the CMake `flash` target,
`cmake --build --preset <preset> --target flash`.

### Choosing a flash tool

| `FLASH_TOOL` | Program | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `openocd` (default) | `openocd` | Use another probe with `-DOPENOCD_INTERFACE=<name>` (any config under OpenOCD's `interface/`) |
| `stlink` | `st-flash` | Open-source stlink tools (`brew install stlink`); writes the `.bin` at `0x08000000` |
| `cubeprog` | `STM32_Programmer_CLI` | ST's STM32CubeProgrammer; found in its default install location even if not on PATH |

Switch with:

```sh
make configure FLASH_TOOL=stlink        # or: cmake --preset {{ boards[0] }} -DFLASH_TOOL=stlink
```

The choice is stored in that board's CMake cache, so later `make flash` keeps
using it until you switch again or run `make clean`. To change the default
for everyone, edit `FLASH_TOOL` in `src/CMakeLists.txt`.

With the default tool, `make flash` runs:

```sh
{% for b in boards -%}
# {{ b }}
openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/{{ board_meta[b]['openocd'] }}.cfg \
  -c "program build/{{ b }}/{{ project_slug }}.elf verify reset exit"
{% endfor %}```

